<!--BlockML Documentation — update A02 page skeletons
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.task.A02_02_UpdatePageSkeletons-->
<task:A02_02_UpdatePageSkeletons xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:task="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.task"
  xmlns:workflow="org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow"
  xmlns:source="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.lib.source"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">

  <baseType>
    workflow:InstructionTask
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A task that updates A02 page skeletons
  </is>
  <documentation>
    A02 structuring task: PagePlan.scope names the topic only.

    - **Sources** — read authorativeSources and select the SSOT Blocks that
      cover each page's scope
    - **Skeleton** — write a formulated purpose plus see links to those sources
    - **Overwrite** — an existing skeleton is replaced; its content is never
      used as input
    - **Body** — page body content stays for a03
  </documentation>
  <properties>
    <instructions type="type:Text" override="true">
      <value>
        <![CDATA[
          PagePlan carries name plus planning fields. scope is what the page
          covers — not a purpose, title, or outline. readerOutcome,
          learningObjective, exclusion, and supportingPoint refine the
          intent. Structuring must open the authoritative sources, choose
          the SSOT Blocks that cover scope, and write a formulated purpose
          from what those Blocks actually say.

          1. Read the plan
          Read org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a01_planning.data.BmlDocSetPlan. Walk every nested
          PagePlan under rootPageGroupPlan. Ignore PageGroupPlan entries.

          2. Open the authoritative sources before writing a page
          Resolve this task's authorativeSources TypeSelectors (scan type for each
          selector). Also read BmlDocSetPlan.authoritativeSources (the core Library and
          the Blocks it owns). For each candidate, inspect is, documentation, and
          references — do not guess from the FQN or from scope alone.

          3. Bind sources to scope
          For each PagePlan, select the source Blocks whose documented subject matches
          that page's scope. Those selected Blocks are the page's authoritative
          sources. Every page must have at least one Requires source. If several
          sources match, Requires = primary SSOT for the scope; SeeAlso = supporting
          background. Do not attach a source that does not serve the scope.

          4. Formulate the skeleton from the bound sources
          The a02 subpackages data, page, and pagegroup
          (org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data,
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page,
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.pagegroup) are created
          by A02_01_UpdateDocSet if they do not already exist. This task does not
          create those packages.

          Resolve the A02 FQN as
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page + "." + PagePlan.name
          (for example docs.FirstBlock →
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page.docs.FirstBlock).
          Do not write in page packages of other sectors — only this a02
          page package, never a page package outside a02 (a03 or any later
          sector). Do not create or edit pages outside a02, PageGroups,
          or pageMapping.

          If a skeleton with that name already exists, discard its current content
          and regenerate the file from the plan and the bound authoritative sources.
          Existing skeleton content is never authoritative: do not treat it as true,
          and do not use it as input for generation (not is, documentation, purpose,
          title, see links, or any other field). Keep only the FQN / file path so
          the same Block is overwritten. Do not invent pages that are not in the plan.

          Write purpose as a finished renderer instruction: why this page exists and
          what it must accomplish, grounded in the bound sources (their is /
          documentation / claims). Do not copy scope into purpose and do not leave
          purpose as a topic list.

          Each skeleton must:
          - use baseType org.blockml.bml.docgen.page.DocPage
            (not org.blockml.bml.docgen.core.Page)
          - set is to one short identity sentence informed by the bound sources
          - set documentation to name the scope, name the bound source FQNs, and
            state that body content is authored in a03 from those sources
          - override title, purpose, detailLevel (org.blockml.bml.docgen.level.*),
            and pageType (org.blockml.bml.docgen.pagetype.*) from the bound sources
          - list each bound source as references/see (Requires or SeeAlso)
          - omit every aggregation, including DocPage.content and Page.rules /
            authoritativeSources / audiences / semantic lists. Do not author
            sections, paragraphs, or other page body
          - omit docset

          5. Register every A02 page on BmlDocSet_A02
          Update org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.BmlDocSet_A02.
          Put every A02 skeleton written in this task into BmlDocSet_A02.pages
          (TypeReferenceEntity links, plan order). Do not invent pages that are
          not in the plan.

          Set BmlDocSet_A02.homePage from BmlDocSetPlan.homePage, resolved to
          the matching A02 page FQN (a02 page package + the planned page name,
          for example docs.TableOfContents →
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page.docs.TableOfContents).
          homePage must be one of the a02 pages in pages.

          BmlDocSet_A02.pages and homePage may contain only a02 pages. Never
          insert or keep a page from another sector (a03 or later). If an
          existing pages entry is outside a02, remove it. Do not edit DocSets
          of other sectors.

          Export each A02 skeleton from org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.Library if it is not
          already in the catalog. Do not remove a03 catalog entries.
        ]]>
      </value>
    </instructions>
  </properties>
  <aggregations>
    <authorativeSources override="true">
      <composition>
        <source:BlockMLSourceSet />
      </composition>
    </authorativeSources>
  </aggregations>
</task:A02_02_UpdatePageSkeletons>
